  description="China to Greece freight guide: 24% VAT on EU common duty, Piraeus GRPIR the COSCO-run gateway, ~33–40-day Cape sea transit and the Suez-routing inversion."
  canonical={pageUrl}
  ogType="article"
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb
        items={[
          { label: 'Europe', href: '/europe/' },
          { label: 'Shipping from China to Greece' },
        ]}
      />
      <span class="badge badge--amber">September 2026 updated</span>
      <h1>Shipping from China to Greece: Piraeus GRPIR gateway, 24% VAT, and the COSCO-owned Med hub question</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A one-page freight brief for importers moving cargo from Shanghai, Ningbo-Zhoushan, Shenzhen
        and the wider China origin set to Piraeus and Thessaloniki — with the two-port geography,
        the roughly 33–40-day sea window via the Cape (and the 22–28-day Suez alternative that
        inverts it), EU common duty plus 24% VAT, the EORI gate, the COSCO-owned Piraeus hub, and the
        hidden destination charges that shape the Greek landed cost.
