    <p>
      The China-to-Greece clock has one dominant beat — the <strong>sea leg to Piraeus</strong> — and a
      routing fork that moves it by roughly two weeks. The WorldFreightHub Europe route data puts the
      <strong>Genoa Mediterranean benchmark at ~33 days</strong>, and Piraeus sits further east in the Aegean,
